{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A finite directed graph on the vertices "},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whose out-neighbors come from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure, called on demand and never stored: an implicit graph (Boost’s "},{"code":"grid_graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"GridGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"FullGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). It is a lawful "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so every generic algorithm runs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on it, including those that need the whole vertex set (components, centrality), with no edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST","text":"Sequence","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For a state space with no vertex collection (an unbounded grid, a puzzle), use the closure","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"searches instead: Traversal’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"breadthFirstSearch(from:successors:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ShortestPaths’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"dijkstraShortestPath(from:cutoff:successors:success:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"aStarShortestPath(from:cutoff: successors:heuristic:success:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" states over a finite set, number them and use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LabeledGraph<State, ImplicitDirectedGraph<Row>>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; a grid is numbered row-major.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The closure."}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(v)"},{"text":" lists the targets of the edges leaving ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"text":", once per edge, as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence<Int>"},{"text":" (an array, a lazy filter over a fixed neighbor list), so a specialized build","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inlines it with no type erasure. Each read of a row calls it once: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges(of:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outDegree(of:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"text":" once each, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeCount"},{"text":" once","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per vertex. It must return the same sequence each time it is asked about the same vertex (the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"protocol’s “asking again gives the same answer”); this is documented, not checked, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"closure that breaks it breaks every algorithm, as a mutating ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"text":" breaks ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Set"},{"text":". Each target is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"checked to be a vertex when it is read, not when the row is formed.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On a hot path, return a small struct that computes the row up front into fixed slots and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"yields them by count, rather than a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lazy.filter"},{"text":" over a fixed neighbor list: the filter calls","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its predicate per element and keeps the unfiltered iterator’s state, and in the benchmarks on a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1000 × 1000 grid it cost 1.2–1.8× the precomputed row (breadth-first layers, components,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Dijkstra).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Positions."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" An edge’s position is "},{"code":"Edges.Index","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": its source, its rank in the source’s row,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and its target. Equality, order and hashing use "},{"code":"(source, rank)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", unique even among parallel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edges and self-loops; the target rides along, so "},{"code":"source(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"target(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"weight closure reading "},{"code":"$0.target","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" call nothing. There are no dense edge indices."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Not ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": a closure has no identity and is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s9EscapableP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14ImplicitGraphs0A13DirectedGraphV","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","modules":[{"name":"ImplicitGraphs"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift#L38"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"}]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/OutEdges","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/Successors"],"anchor":"Structures","generated":true,"title":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/init(vertexCount:successors:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/DirectedGraph-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://ImplicitGraphs/documentation/ImplicitGraphs":{"type":"topic","title":"ImplicitGraphs","url":"\/documentation\/implicitgraphs","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs","abstract":[]},"doc://ImplicitGraphs/documentation/ImplicitGraphs/ImplicitDirectedGraph":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph","abstract":[{"text":"A finite directed graph on the vertices ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"text":" whose out-neighbors come from a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"closure, called on demand and never stored: an implicit graph (Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"grid_graph"},{"text":", LEMON’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GridGraph"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FullGraph"},{"text":"). It is a lawful ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"text":", so every generic algorithm runs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on it, including those that need the whole vertex set (components, centrality), with no edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"storage.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://ImplicitGraphs/documentation/ImplicitGraphs/ImplicitDirectedGraph/DirectedGraph-Implementations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[],"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph\/directedgraph-implementations","title":"DirectedGraph Implementations"},"doc://ImplicitGraphs/s9EscapableP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s9EscapableP","title":"Swift.Escapable"},"doc://ImplicitGraphs/documentation/ImplicitGraphs/ImplicitDirectedGraph/OutEdges":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The positions of the edges leaving one vertex, in row order: ranks 0, 1, …, each with its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"target, checked to be a vertex as it is read."}],"role":"symbol","title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph.OutEdges","identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/OutEdges","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OutEdges","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OutEdges","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph\/outedges"},"doc://ImplicitGraphs/documentation/ImplicitGraphs/ImplicitDirectedGraph/init(vertexCount:successors:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" whose out-neighbors of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(v)"},{"type":"text","text":". O(1): calls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph\/init(vertexcount:successors:)","kind":"symbol","title":"init(vertexCount:successors:)","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"vertexCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"successors"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Row"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/init(vertexCount:successors:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://ImplicitGraphs/s8CopyableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s8CopyableP","title":"Swift.Copyable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://ImplicitGraphs/documentation/ImplicitGraphs/ImplicitDirectedGraph/Successors":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Successors"}],"type":"topic","title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph.Successors","url":"\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph\/successors","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/Successors","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The closure’s row for one vertex, each target checked to be a vertex as it is read (not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when the row is formed). A struct rather than a lazy map, so an algorithm that keeps an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterator per vertex on its stack (Tarjan’s) allocates nothing for it."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Successors"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","title":"DirectedGraph"}}}